          "tz": -420
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Di Wang",
          "email": "diwa@nvidia.com",
          "date": "2026-11-03 23:26:37.000000000",
          "tz": -480
        },
        "subject": "LU-21061 lmv: migrate directories onto pool MDTs",
        "message": "LU-21061 lmv: migrate directories onto pool MDTs\n\n\"lfs migrate -m -1 -p POOL\" sends the pool to the MDTs, which take the\nother stripes of a directory from it, but the client picks the MDT of\nthe top directory among all MDTs, and nothing checks that the pool\nexists or that a given MDT index is in it.  Rerunning the migration\nalso moves every file and directory again.\n\nIn lmv_migrate(), choose the MDT of a top directory among the MDTs of\na pool that lists MDTs: keep a directory that is on one of them, else\nfollow its parent if that is on one, else choose by space usage.\nName the chosen MDT in the request, so that the MDT skips a file or\nplain directory that is already there, and a rerun finishes an\ninterrupted migration without moving the rest again.  Check the pool\nand the MDT indices in llapi_migrate_mdt() as for mkdir, sharing the\ncheck with verify_dir_param(), and strip a \"fsname.\" prefix from the\npool name in lfs before it is copied into the request.\n\nTest-Parameters: mdscount=2 mdtcount=4 testlist=ost-pools\nTest-Parameters: mdscount=2 mdtcount=4 testlist=sanity env=ONLY=230\nSigned-off-by: Di Wang <diwa@nvidia.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm\nChange-Id: I0898d07d755d6d388e0f4643126174f93c4066aa\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
